  {
    "client_msg_id": "b762b45c-9718-4150-bc41-2cf7831ed484",
    "type": "message",
    "user": "U08RZQ547LJ",
    "text": "\u003e Will this be handled by olake in later versions\nRegarding this, we have never seen such an issue with other catalogs, as none of them had the 1 MB _metadata.json_ limit. BigLake's catalog is also evolving and is still relatively immature.\n\nWe’ll brainstorm this internally over the next week and explore what kind of solution we can implement in OLake-Go so that users don’t have to face this issue, at least when using BigLake.\n\n\nFor now, you’ll have to run / schedule the snapshot expiry script manually.",
    "ts": "1791313012.762179",
    "thread_ts": "1791283377.097869",
    "edited": {
      "user": "U08RZQ547LJ",
      "ts": "1791313078.000000"
